<title>USA: Georgia jobless rate dips to 4.3 pct for December.</title>
<headline>Georgia jobless rate dips to 4.3 pct for December.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's unemployment rate dipped to 4.3 percent in December, unchanged from November and down from 4.5 percnet a year ago, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said Thursday.</p>
<p>Jobless rates were down or unchanged over the month for the state's major metropolitan areas. Rates were:</p>
<p>--Albany, 5.2 percent in December, down from 5.3 percent in November.</p>
<p>--Athens, 2.7 percent, down from 2.8 percent.</p>
<p>--Atlanta, 3.6 percent, unchanged.</p>
<p>--Augusta, 5.9 percent, down from 6.2 percent.</p>
<p>--Columbus, 4.3 percent, down from 4.5 percent.</p>
<p>((Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
